.TH "XMLHTTPREQUESTEVENTTARGET.LOADSTART_EVENT" "3JS" "July 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
XMLHttpRequestEventTarget.loadstart_event \- XMLHttpRequestEventTarget:
loadstart event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers, except for
Service Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]loadstart\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when a request has
started to load data.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqloadstart\(dq, (event) => { })

onloadstart = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]ProgressEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Usage with XMLHttpRequest
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]div\f[R] class=\(dqcontrols\(dq>
  <\f[B]input\f[R]
    class=\(dqxhr success\(dq
    type=\(dqbutton\(dq
    name=\(dqxhr\(dq
    value=\(dqClick to start XHR (success)\(dq />
  <\f[B]input\f[R]
    class=\(dqxhr error\(dq
    type=\(dqbutton\(dq
    name=\(dqxhr\(dq
    value=\(dqClick to start XHR (error)\(dq />
  <\f[B]input\f[R]
    class=\(dqxhr abort\(dq
    type=\(dqbutton\(dq
    name=\(dqxhr\(dq
    value=\(dqClick to start XHR (abort)\(dq />
</\f[B]div\f[R]>

<\f[B]textarea\f[R] readonly class=\(dqevent\-log\(dq></\f[B]textarea\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] xhrButtonSuccess = document.querySelector(\(dq.xhr.success\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] xhrButtonError = document.querySelector(\(dq.xhr.error\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] xhrButtonAbort = document.querySelector(\(dq.xhr.abort\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] log = document.querySelector(\(dq.event\-log\(dq);

\f[B]function\f[R] handleEvent(e) {
  log.textContent = \(ga${log.textContent}${e.type}: ${e.loaded} bytes transferred\(rsn\(ga;
}

\f[B]function\f[R] addListeners(xhr) {
  xhr.addEventListener(\(dqloadstart\(dq, handleEvent);
  xhr.addEventListener(\(dqload\(dq, handleEvent);
  xhr.addEventListener(\(dqloadend\(dq, handleEvent);
  xhr.addEventListener(\(dqprogress\(dq, handleEvent);
  xhr.addEventListener(\(dqerror\(dq, handleEvent);
  xhr.addEventListener(\(dqabort\(dq, handleEvent);
}

\f[B]function\f[R] runXHR(url) {
  log.textContent = \(dq\(dq;

  \f[B]const\f[R] xhr = \f[B]new\f[R] XMLHttpRequest();
  addListeners(xhr);
  xhr.open(\(dqGET\(dq, url);
  xhr.send();
  \f[B]return\f[R] xhr;
}

xhrButtonSuccess.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  runXHR(\(dqexample\-image.jpg\(dq);
});

xhrButtonError.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  runXHR(\(dqhttps://example.com/notfound.jpg\(dq);
});

xhrButtonAbort.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  runXHR(\(dqexample\-image.jpg\(dq).abort();
});
.EE
.SS Result
.SS Usage with XMLHttpRequestUpload
You can use the \f[CR]loadstart\f[R] event to detect the beginning of an
upload.
For a complete code example that uploads a file and displays a progress
bar, see the main \f[CR]XMLHttpRequestUpload\f[R] page.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// When the upload starts, we display the progress bar\f[R]
xhr.upload.addEventListener(\(dqloadstart\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  progressBar.classList.add(\(dqvisible\(dq);
  progressBar.value = 0;
  progressBar.max = event.total;
  log.textContent = \(dqUploading (0%)\&...\(dq;
  abortButton.disabled = \f[B]false\f[R];
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
